  "notes": [
    "Four variants with different steps, CFG and licence: name one. The family-level profile, used when no variant is named, carries only what they share.",
    "Base steps: BFL's card and the Diffusers default give 50, sd.cpp's example 20. The profile takes 50, because the step count is a property of the model rather than a backend convention; sd.cpp's 20 is a faster example.",
    "Base sampler: no source names one, so the route's own default applies. The distilled variants use sd.cpp's euler.",
    "Licence: the 4B models are Apache-2.0, the 9B models FLUX Non-Commercial.",
    "A 9B KV variant also exists; the research gives no settings for it, so it has no profile variant yet.",
    "sd.cpp passes edit references with -r."
  ]
